<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!--
	The zombie clan as a proper XML faction instead of a clan built at runtime.

	Copied from the vanilla mercenary minor faction "ghilman" (SandBox/ModuleData/
	spclans.xml). Going through XML deserialization means the game initializes
	everything Clan.Deserialize normally sets - banner colors, minor faction
	template list, tier, renown - which a Clan.CreateClan() clan never gets. That
	missing initialization is what the debug ladder pinned down (t0 vanilla clan
	worked, t1 our runtime clan crashed).

	Deviations from the ghilman original, deliberately kept minimal:
	  id / name / text          - ours
	  culture                   - looters, matching our troops and the bandit look
	  default_party_template    - our horde template
	  color / color2            - green
	  is_clan_type_mercenary    - dropped, zombies do not hire out as mercenaries
	  initial_home_settlement   - a hideout instead of a castle, no ownership implied
	  minor_faction_character_templates - omitted on purpose: we want no hero lords.
	                              Vanilla bandit factions omit it too, so the list
	                              ends up empty rather than null.
	  is_minor_faction          - REMOVED, replaced by is_bandit + is_outlaw.
	Everything else (banner_key, settlement_banner_mesh, tier) is taken over verbatim.

	Why bandit instead of minor faction: a minor faction is expected to have lords,
	and vanilla's daily minor-faction upkeep ran into our heroless clan (the game
	already flagged the party as "wrongly created" in the conversation system, and
	the crash landed in the daily tick). The bandit faction is the one vanilla
	archetype that is heroless, owns parties and is hostile to everyone - exactly
	what a zombie horde is. IsBanditFaction also keeps the clan out of all the
	noble-clan logic (finances, diplomacy, succession) that assumes a leader exists.

	The vanilla bandit auto-spawn stays inert for us: SpawnLooters only runs off
	infested hideouts owned by the clan (we own none, so its count goes negative and
	the loop never executes), and hideouts are only ever assigned to clans whose
	culture has can_have_settlement="true" - the looters culture does not.
-->
<Factions>
	<Faction
		id="zombie_horde"
		initial_home_settlement="Settlement.hideout_mountain_2"
		banner_key="11.191.154.1536.1536.764.764.1.0.0.401.116.155.488.488.764.764.0.0.0"
		color="FF3D8B3D"
		color2="FF1F4D1F"
		culture="Culture.looters"
		default_party_template="PartyTemplate.zombie_horde_template"
		settlement_banner_mesh="encounter_flag_f"
		is_bandit="true"
		is_outlaw="true"
		name="{=zombieplague_clan_name}Zombie Horde"
		tier="4"
		text="{=zombieplague_clan_text}A growing horde of the risen dead. They do not negotiate, they do not retreat, and every fight they win makes them larger."></Faction>
</Factions>
